      "content": "that's a really strong starting point for my paper. to make the argument even more robust, i want to address the inevitable pushback from those who argue that this \"presumptive privilege\" basically creates a black box that prevents any real accountability. how should i technically frame the rebuttal to the idea that a broader privilege is just a way to hide potential wrongdoing or corruption from the public eye?",
